#################################################################



#################################################################
#  v9.75.0 (2026-09-09, brsf-session) -- THE OBLIGATIONS DO NOT BIND
#  THE LINEAGE THAT BUILDS THEM. Owner's rule, this day: "apply the
#  rulings only after the completion of the work and the lineage is
#  closed. You should never try to apply a new ruling when the
#  development is in progress."
#
#  The first draft of shapes v1.111.0 bound every lineage. Its first
#  run refused fw:Out_Goal_SDLC (published 629b62f) and four fixture
#  lineages and every toy of the exercise register -- work already
#  finished or in flight under rules that did not exist when it was
#  done. That is the same failure the owner named in an earlier
#  session, and the session repeated it. Corrected before release:
#  an obligation binds only a lineage that ADOPTED its set at the
#  moment it opened (adoptsObligationSet + adoptionRecordedAtOpen,
#  in the Mission stage's own commit), and ObligationAdoptionShape
#  refuses adoption by a lineage past LS_Opened. Lineage 9 is past
#  LS_Goaled; it therefore does not adopt and owes nothing new. The
#  first lineage OPENED after these obligations ship will be the
#  first to owe them.
#
#  Imp_SDLCArtifactKinds is RESOLVED BY FINDING: the four artifact
#  kinds requested from another registrant (1b65620) already existed in this
#  framework's own TBox -- ModelKind's fourteen UML 2.5 kinds,
