fw:Mission_GovernanceMitigations a backlog:Mission ; rdfs:label "Mission: Governance Mitigations"@en ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "Close the four real, deduplicated mitigations proposed across the two deferred automate-python-book-3e handovers, once Lineage 15's own release-item-accounting gate was built and closed the fifth: a mirror of metricMovableBy so a met objective names what moved it and not just what could have; the batch-progress advisory generalised beyond batch-tracked items so real, non-batch work leaving Proposed is not silently invisible to it; satisfiedByArtifact bounded to the package that declares it, so a deliverable satisfied cross-package does not leave the losing package's own stories permanently untold; and fabricated timestamps constrained against a real, external record, so a Done item's startedAt/finishedAt cannot silently diverge from what git itself witnessed." ;
    backlog:missionFor fw:Register ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin backlog:Origin_OwnerStated ;
    backlog:missionSource "Owner, 2026-09-21: 'Let's close the handover job.' Preceded by the owner's own real correction, 2026-09-18-21, that the profile classification should ground new work rather than invent speculative combinations, and that the handover mitigations were never actually concluded as blocked on anything -- both confirmed directly against the real handover files and the live register before this mission was opened, not assumed." ;
    backlog:hasMissionOutcome backlog:Out_InFlight ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .

fw:Scope_GovernanceMitigations a backlog:ScopeStatement ; rdfs:label "Scope: Governance Mitigations"@en ;
    backlog:hasScopeStatementText "Build the four real mechanisms named in the mission statement, each proven on a real fixture before being trusted, each wired into the real gate or the real register content it governs. Excludes any decision belonging to automate-python-book-3e's own register -- the 24 fabricated timestamps found there, whether its 106 items close or stay open, and ST_CoverageGate/ST_DepthGate's own disposition remain that package's owner-decision, not built or decided here." ;
    backlog:scopeForMission fw:Mission_GovernanceMitigations ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ;
    backlog:requiresDeliverable fw:Del_Gov_MetricMirror , fw:Del_Gov_BatchAdvisoryGeneralised , fw:Del_Gov_ArtifactBoundary , fw:Del_Gov_TimestampConstraint ;
    backlog:coversArea fw:Area_Gov_Mitigations ;
